## Overview: The Global Vaccine Landscape
Since the emergence of SARS-CoV-2, over 10 vaccine platforms have received regulatory authorization. Clinical trial Vaccine Efficacy (VE) and real-world effectiveness demonstrate high initial protection, though viral variants (Delta/Omicron) and waning immunity have necessitated sophisticated booster strategies.

---

## 📊 Comparative Efficacy Matrix

| Vaccine Platform | Phase III VE (Wild-type) | Real-World Effectiveness (Delta) | Omicron Performance |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **mRNA-1273 (Moderna)** | **94.1%** | 86% Infection / 93% Hosp. | 71% (2-dose) / 86% (Boosted) |
| **BNT162b2 (Pfizer)** | **95.0%** | 91% Infection / 94% Hosp. | 88% after 2 doses (Severe) |
| **NVX-CoV2373 (Novavax)** | **89.7%** | 86-90% Infection | ~50% (2-dose) / ~80% (Boosted) |
| **ChAdOx1 (AstraZeneca)** | **70.4%** | 80-85% Hospitalization | ~30% (2-dose) / ~70% (Boosted) |
| **Ad26.COV2.S (J&J)** | **66.9%** | 71% Infection / 93% Hosp. | 30-40% (1-dose) / ~70% (Boosted) |
| **Inactivated (Sinovac)** | **50-60%** | 65-70% (Severe) | Substantially Reduced |

---

## 🔬 Maverick Technical Analysis

### 1. The mRNA Advantage
The high-potency mRNA platforms (Pfizer/Moderna) remain the gold standard for neutralizing antibody induction. Moderna's higher antigen concentration (100µg vs 30µg in Pfizer) correlates with 1.5–2x higher neutralizing titres, particularly beneficial in elderly populations where immunosenescence is a factor.

### 2. Adenoviral Vector Waning
Waning is more pronounced in adenoviral platforms (AZ/J&J) compared to mRNA. **Heterologous mRNA boosting** (switching platforms) is now the standard of care, often yielding superior immunogenicity compared to homologous schedules.

### 3. Safety Profile Summary:
*   **mRNA:** Myocarditis/pericarditis risk (≈12-45/million), primarily in young males.
*   **Adenoviral:** Rare Thrombosis with Thrombocytopenia Syndrome (TTS) (≈2-6/million).
*   **Inactivated:** High safety profil but rapid efficacy decay after 4-5 months.

---

> [!TIP]
> **Maverick Recommendation:**
> 3-dose mRNA series restores >90% protection against severe disease even with Omicron BA.5 variants. Heterologous boosting is highly recommended for those initially vaccinated with vector-based or inactivated platforms.

